---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
import MediaFigure from '../../components/MediaFigure.astro';
import { ASSETS } from '../../data/assets';
import { CHAPTERS } from '../../data/chapter-guide';

const title = 'Resonance: A Plague Tale Legacy Weapons';
const description =
  'Resonance: A Plague Tale Legacy weapons: the eight Blades and where each one is, the Heritage Pack Minoan Sword, the Grapnel, the Minoan sphere, and throwables.';
const crumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'Weapons', url: '/weapons/' },
];
const bladeChapters = CHAPTERS.filter((c) => c.blade);
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} pageType="collection" breadcrumbs={crumbs}>
  <div class="container py-10">
    <Breadcrumb items={crumbs} />
    <header class="mt-6 max-w-3xl">
      <p class="section-kicker">Loadout</p>
      <h1 class="section-title">Resonance: A Plague Tale Legacy weapons</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-lg text-fog">
        Sophia fights in melee. Her swords are the eight Blades, collected one per chapter through Chapter 10;
        the Grapnel, the Minoan sphere and throwables round out the kit.
      </p>
    </header>
    <div class="mt-8"><MediaFigure {...ASSETS.weaponBlade} /></div>

    <div class="prose-page mt-10 max-w-3xl">
      <h2>Melee first</h2>
      <p>
        The Steam description frames Resonance around dynamic, violent melee: agility, tricks, sharp reflexes,
        perfected parries and powerful strikes. Fights are read through attack colours — parry a normal swing,
        parry a yellow attack for a counter, dodge a red one unless you have the mastery that lets Sophia parry
        red. The <a href="/combat/">combat guide</a> covers the rhythm; this page covers what you fight with.
      </p>

      <h2>The eight Blades</h2>
      <p>
        Blades come from the Heroes’ Graves, the bull-pillar crypts off the main route. The first two are handed
        to you; the rest need a short detour, usually a light-alignment puzzle at a bull pillar. Chapters 11 to
        14 have none, so the set is complete once you leave Parallel Paths.
      </p>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Blade</th>
            <th scope="col">Chapter</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {bladeChapters.map((c) => (
            <tr>
              <td>{c.blade!.name}</td>
              <td><a href={`/walkthrough/${c.slug}/`}>{c.number}. {c.title}</a></td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>
        Equip them from the Sophia menu, under your skills, alongside Charms. You can swap freely; there is no
        upgrade tree to lose. Step-by-step locations are on{' '}
        <a href="/plague-tale-legacy-all-blade-locations/">all eight Blade locations</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Blade achievements</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Plunderer</strong> — collect all Blades from the Heroes’ Graves.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Adaptable</strong> — get one kill with each Blade. Switch to a newly found sword before the next
          camp fight and the list clears itself during the story.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Neither is missable: Blades count in Story Select after the credits, and the chapter menu shows how many
        you found in each chapter.
      </p>

      <h2>The Heritage Pack Minoan Sword</h2>
      <p>
        The Minoan Sword comes with the $3.99 Heritage Pack DLC. Every third hit lands a powerful strike that
        stuns. It does not count toward Plunderer or Adaptable, so treat it as a convenience rather than a ninth
        grave Blade. One related bug: the Falchion could disappear from the inventory after a DLC install — the
        October update lists that as fixed. See <a href="/resonance-falchion-after-dlc/">Falchion missing after
        the DLC</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Grapnel</h2>
      <p>
        The Grapnel is picked up in Chapter 2, at the same barrel by the boat that gives you the Falchion. It is a
        traversal tool first, but the game leans on it later: you Grapnel up to the bull statue for the Xiphos in
        Chapter 10, and the final fight against Asterion uses it to break the statue’s cracked heart and mouth.
      </p>

      <h2>Minoan sphere</h2>
      <p>
        Sophia’s stolen Minoan sphere manipulates light. On this site it is treated as a puzzle and route tool,
        not a damage weapon: it opens bull pillars (the Khopesh in Chapter 7 is behind one) and aligns coloured
        lights on pillar gems. The <a href="/minoan-sphere-light-puzzle-guide/">Minoan sphere guide</a> covers the
        puzzles.
      </p>

      <h2>Throwables and the environment</h2>
      <p>
        Throwables are pickups you find during fights. Bottles stun — shielded enemies can block them — and a
        throwing knife kills an archer in one hit, according to a community achievement guide on Steam. Ledges
        are a weapon too: enemies pushed down a drop die, and the October 6 update fixed enemies that survived
        being pushed off an edge. Three achievements track this — Returning the favor, No holds barred and
        Overboard — covered on the <a href="/resonance-overboard-throwable-achievements/">throwable achievements
        guide</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Focus attacks and critical strikes</h2>
      <p>
        Two named attack types show up in the achievement list: critical strikes (Sharp enough for you? asks for
        25 critical-strike kills) and Focus attacks (Inherited brutality asks for four enemies killed at once with
        one). Before the October bug-fix update the Focus Attack input could not be changed; the update lists that
        lock as fixed. See{' '}
        <a href="/resonance-focus-prism-input-planning/">Focus Attack and Prism controls</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-8 text-sm text-fog">
      Skills that change how these weapons play:{' '}
      <a href="/plague-tale-legacy-skills-unlock-order/" class="text-wheat underline">skills unlock order</a>.
      Every collectible set: <a href="/plague-tale-legacy-collectibles-by-chapter/" class="text-wheat underline">collectibles by chapter</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
